[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:The Channel Tunnel]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.00]Why was the first tunnel not completed? | 为什么第一条隧道没有建成？
[00:14.67]In 1858, a French engineer, Aime Thome de Gamond, | 1858年，一位法国工程师埃梅·托姆·德·干蒙
[00:20.80]arrived in England with a plan for a 21-mile tunnel under the English Channel. | 到达英国，带着一份在英吉利海峡下面开凿一条21英里隧道的计划。
[00:27.69]He said that it would be possible to build a platform in the centre of the Channel. | 他说可以在海峡中央建一座平台。
[00:34.17]This platform would serve as a port and a railway station. | 这座平台将用作港口和火车站。
[00:39.63]The tunnel would be well-ventilated if tall chimneys were built above sea level. | 如果建造高出海面的高烟囱，隧道就会通风良好。
[00:46.35]In 1860, a better plan was put forward by an Englishman, William Low. | 1860年，一位英国人威廉·洛提出了一个更好的方案。
[00:53.93]He suggested that a double railway-tunnel should be built. | 他建议修建一条双轨隧道。
[00:58.66]This would solve the problem of ventilation for if a train entered this tunnel, it would draw in fresh air behind it. | 这将解决通风问题，因为如果一列火车开进隧道，它后面就会带进新鲜空气。
[01:08.89]Forty-two years later a tunnel was actually begun. | 42年后隧道真的开始动工了。
[01:13.97]If, at the time, the British had not feared invasion, it would have been completed. | 如果当时英国人不怕入侵，隧道早就建成了。
[01:22.13]The world had to wait almost another 100 years for the Channel Tunnel. | 世界不得不为英吉利海峡隧道再等待将近100年。
[01:28.61]It was officially opened on March 7, 1994, finally connecting Britain to the European continent. | 它于1994年3月7日正式开通，最终将英国与欧洲大陆连接了起来。
